The  driver  supports  the Silicon Image SATALink 3112 2‐port and
3114 4‐port Serial ATA controllers, and  provides  the  interface
with  the  hardware  for  the driver.  The 0x0002 flag forces the
driver to disable DMA on chipsets for which DMA would normally be
enabled.  This can be used as a debugging aid, or to work  around
problems  where the SATA controller is wired up to the system in‐
correctly.
